---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { bySlug, destMonthUrl, deg, MONTHS } from '../../lib/data';

// Typical flowering windows; they shift with each year's rain and temperatures.
const spots: { slug: string; place: string; flowers: string; when: string; m: number }[] = [
  { slug: 'death-valley', place: 'Death Valley & the California deserts', flowers: 'Desert gold, poppies and verbena — a "superbloom" only after a wet winter', when: 'Late February – April', m: 2 },
  { slug: 'joshua-tree', place: 'Joshua Tree & Anza-Borrego', flowers: 'Desert wildflowers and blooming cacti', when: 'March – April', m: 2 },
  { slug: 'crete', place: 'Crete', flowers: 'Wild orchids, anemones and poppies on the hillsides', when: 'March – April', m: 3 },
  { slug: 'austin', place: 'Texas Hill Country', flowers: 'Bluebonnets and Indian paintbrush along the roadsides', when: 'Late March – mid-April', m: 3 },
  { slug: 'amsterdam', place: 'The Netherlands', flowers: 'Tulip fields around Lisse and Keukenhof gardens', when: 'Mid-April – early May', m: 3 },
  { slug: 'kyoto', place: 'Japan', flowers: 'Cherry blossoms, then azaleas and wisteria', when: 'Late March – May', m: 3 },
  { slug: 'provence', place: 'Provence', flowers: 'Lavender fields on the Valensole plateau and around Sénanque Abbey', when: 'Late June – late July', m: 6 },
  { slug: 'hokkaido', place: 'Hokkaido (Furano)', flowers: 'Lavender and patchwork flower fields', when: 'July', m: 6 },
  { slug: 'switzerland', place: 'The Swiss Alps', flowers: 'Alpine meadows of gentians, edelweiss and alpenrose', when: 'June – August', m: 6 },
  { slug: 'dolomites', place: 'The Dolomites', flowers: 'High meadows on the Alpe di Siusi and Seceda', when: 'Late June – July', m: 6 },
  { slug: 'glacier-national-park', place: 'Glacier National Park', flowers: 'Beargrass, glacier lilies and paintbrush along Going-to-the-Sun Road', when: 'Late June – August', m: 6 },
  { slug: 'mount-rainier', place: 'Mount Rainier', flowers: 'Lupine, paintbrush and avalanche lilies in the Paradise meadows', when: 'Late July – mid-August', m: 7 },
  { slug: 'cape-town', place: 'Namaqualand & the West Coast (from Cape Town)', flowers: 'Orange and white daisies carpeting the semi-desert', when: 'Mid-August – September', m: 7 },
  { slug: 'perth', place: 'Western Australia', flowers: 'Kangaroo paw, everlastings and orchids — over 12,000 species', when: 'August – October', m: 8 },
];
const rows = spots.map((s) => ({ ...s, d: bySlug.get(s.slug)! }));
const byMonth = MONTHS.map((name, m) => ({ name, items: rows.filter((r) => r.m === m) })).filter((x) => x.items.length);
---

<Guide slug="wildflower-seasons" photo="provence">
  <p>
    Wildflower displays follow the rain. In deserts, a wet winter can trigger a spectacular <strong>superbloom</strong> in early
    spring; in the mountains, flowers burst out as the snow melts in early summer; and in Mediterranean climates, hillsides are
    covered in colour from March to May before the summer drought. Here's when and where to go, with the weather to expect.
  </p>

  <h2>Wildflower calendar</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col" class="left">What blooms</th><th scope="col" class="left">When</th><th scope="col">Weather then</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={r.d.url}>{r.place}</a></th>
              <td class="left">{r.flowers}</td>
              <td class="left">{r.when}</td>
              <td><a href={destMonthUrl(r.d, r.m)}>{deg(r.d.months[r.m].high)} / {deg(r.d.months[r.m].low)}</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">Average daily high / low in the peak month, from official climate normals.</p>

  <h2>Month by month</h2>
  <ul>
    {byMonth.map(({ name, items }) => <li><b>{name}:</b> {items.map((r) => r.place).join(', ')}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Desert superblooms</h2>
  <p>
    In the deserts of California and the American Southwest, mass blooms only happen after a wet autumn and winter, and only
    every few years. When they do, Death Valley, Anza-Borrego and the Antelope Valley poppy reserve fill with colour from late
    February (low deserts) into April (higher areas). Park websites post bloom reports each spring. Go early in the morning,
    stay on trails and never pick flowers. See <a href="/destinations/death-valley/">Death Valley</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/destinations/joshua-tree/">Joshua Tree</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Alpine meadows</h2>
  <p>
    In the Alps and the Rockies, the flower season starts in the valleys in late May and climbs with the snowline, peaking in
    high meadows in July. It's also the best time for hiking, with mountain huts and cable cars open. See{' '}
    <a href="/best-time-to-visit-alps/">the Alps</a> and <a href="/best-time-to-visit-rocky-mountains/">the Rocky Mountains</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Namaqualand and Western Australia</h2>
  <p>
    The southern hemisphere's spring brings two of the world's great flower shows. In South Africa, Namaqualand — a 5–6 hour
    drive north of Cape Town, with the West Coast National Park closer at about 90 minutes — is carpeted in daisies from
    mid-August to September. Flowers open in sunshine, so visit between about 10 a.m. and 4 p.m. In Western Australia, the
    wildflower season moves south from the outback in July to Perth and the south-west in September and October.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Check bloom reports:</b> timing moves by weeks from year to year.</li>
    <li><b>Go midweek</b> — popular fields (tulips, lavender, superblooms) get very busy at weekends.</li>
    <li>For trees rather than flowers, see <a href="/guides/cherry-blossom-season/">cherry blossom season</a> and the <a href="/guides/fall-foliage/">fall foliage guide</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
